WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.333
MORCA learns which denoising steps can reuse cached
computation in video diffusion.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.560
A target speedup sets the reuse budget.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:15.837
In this example, latent features and step-error
signals guide 32 reuses across 50 denoising steps.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.511
Offline implicit Q-learning starts from random cache
schedules.

00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:27.638
Online fine-tuning adds fresh rollouts. The reward
is the final video’s fidelity to its uncached
reference.

00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:33.753
Watch the cow’s coat. MORCA keeps the
black-and-white markings in the uncached reference.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:37.809
On CogVideoX, compare the curve of the cup handle.

00:00:39.737 --> 00:00:46.009
Across 200 VBench prompts, MORCA improves PSNR over
SeaCache on all three models.

00:00:46.139 --> 00:00:50.384
The largest gain is 2.82 decibels on CogVideoX.
